	regionKind = "city",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Darnassus is the capital of the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link}, a city of living wood and moonlit water in the high boughs of {link:teldrassil}Teldrassil{/link}. Its halls are grown rather than built. Its terraces open onto gardens and quiet pools, and the {link:temple-of-the-moon}Temple of the Moon{/link} shines at its heart. It is a young city of an ancient people. The kaldorei raised it after the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, when they had lost their immortality and their old home on {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link} lay scarred, and they meant it to be a new beginning.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[When the war against the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} was over, Arch Druid {link:fandral-staghelm}Fandral Staghelm{/link} and his druids grew {link:teldrassil}Teldrassil{/link} beyond the northern coast. Darnassus rose in its crown. The priestesses of Elune took up their temple there, the druids their enclave, and the {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} their barracks. From {link:rut-theran-village}Rut'theran Village{/link} far below, a portal carries travellers up to the city.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Two leaders sit in Darnassus. {link:tyrande-whisperwind}High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind{/link} rules the city and its people as Elune wills. {link:fandral-staghelm}Fandral Staghelm{/link} leads the druids in the long absence of {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion Stormrage{/link}, who has not returned from the {link:emerald-dream}Emerald Dream{/link}. Tyrande asks her people to respect his station, but she reminds them that the affairs of Darnassus are hers alone. Fandral, for his part, trusts no one outside his enclave. He and {link:keeper-remulos}Keeper Remulos{/link} of {link:moonglade}Moonglade{/link} suspect each other of trickery, and the troubles of the World Tree go on unhealed. The {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} keep a sharp watch within the city itself, for something is amiss on {link:teldrassil}Teldrassil{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The priestesses of Elune.{/b} They tend the {link:temple-of-the-moon}Temple of the Moon{/link} and heal the {link:night-elves}kaldorei{/link}.
• {b}The druids of the {link:cenarion-circle}Cenarion Circle{/link}.{/b} They study in the {link:cenarion-enclave}Cenarion Enclave{/link} under the Arch Druid.
• {b}The {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link}.{/b} The warrior-women who guard the city and the forests beyond.
• {b}Allies of the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}.{/b} Dwarven scholars of the {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} and envoys of the {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link} have come to the city.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Founding.{/b} The city was raised in the boughs of the new World Tree after the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}.
• {b}The Moonwells.{/b} The druids of the city draw on the moonwells of {link:teldrassil}Teldrassil{/link}, and messengers carry phials of their water up from {link:shadowglen}Shadowglen{/link}, {link:dolanaar}Dolanaar{/link} and the {link:the-oracle-glade}Oracle Glade{/link}.
• {b}The Rift with {link:moonglade}Moonglade{/link}.{/b} The Arch Druid and {link:keeper-remulos}Keeper Remulos{/link} have grown apart, and the druids of the city serve the Circle under a cloud of suspicion.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The {link:night-elves}kaldorei{/link} have joined the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}, and heroes of every people now walk the terraces of Darnassus.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the City",
			text = [=[• A fountain at the heart of the {link:temple-of-the-moon}Temple of the Moon{/link} holds holy water that is said to purify what it touches.
• The Arch Druid's tree stands in the {link:cenarion-enclave}Cenarion Enclave{/link}, and tunnels run beneath it.
• The druids of Darnassus study soil brought from the far crater of {link:un-goro-crater}Un'Goro{/link}, and they grow herbs from it whose nature they do not yet understand.]=],
		},
	},
})

