			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Tyrande Whisperwind is the High Priestess of Elune and the leader of the night elves. For ten thousand years she has guarded her people, first in the ruins of their ancient empire and now in the boughs of {link:teldrassil}Teldrassil{/link}. She is the beloved of {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion Stormrage{/link}, and she waits for his return. She rules {link:darnassus}Darnassus{/link} firmly, and she is known to be kind.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[Tyrande is the living bond between the {link:night-elves}kaldorei{/link} of old and the kaldorei of today. She fought in the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link} and in the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}. Under her the {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} became the shield of their people, and under her the night elves have joined the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[Tyrande was a novice of the Sisterhood of Elune in the days of {link:queen-azshara}Queen Azshara{/link}. The twin brothers {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion{/link} and {link:illidan-stormrage}Illidan Stormrage{/link} both loved her, and she chose Malfurion. When the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} came, she fought beside them, and she rose to lead the Sisterhood in that war. After the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}, while the druids slept in the {link:emerald-dream}Emerald Dream{/link}, she and her priestesses kept watch over the forests through long centuries.

When the Legion returned and the humans and orcs came to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, Tyrande woke the sleeping druids from their barrow dens. She freed Illidan from his prison, against her beloved's wishes. At the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}, her {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} fought alongside humans and orcs until {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} fell.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion{/link} has gone into the Dream again, and no one knows what has become of him. Tyrande leads the {link:night-elves}kaldorei{/link} alone. She respects {link:fandral-staghelm}Fandral Staghelm{/link} as Arch Druid, but she does not let him forget that his domain is druidism, while hers is the whole of her people. Her priestesses and {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} bring her news from every forest of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, and she hears it herself. Those who come to her temple with deeds done for her people find her grateful and generous, and quick to ask them to share their tales with the young.]=],
